---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { withBase } from "../utils/paths";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Accessibility"
  description="Accessibility statement ownership, review cadence and launch-readiness blockers."
>
  <nav class="govuk-breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
    <ol class="govuk-breadcrumbs__list">
      <li class="govuk-breadcrumbs__list-item">
        <a class="govuk-breadcrumbs__link" href={withBase("/")}>Home</a>
      </li>
      <li class="govuk-breadcrumbs__list-item">Accessibility</li>
    </ol>
  </nav>

  <div class="govuk-grid-row">
    <div class="govuk-grid-column-two-thirds">
      <span class="govuk-caption-l">Launch readiness</span>
      <h1 class="govuk-heading-xl">Accessibility statement</h1>
      <p class="govuk-body-l">
        This page records accessibility statement ownership, review expectations and the remaining
        facts needed before the site can launch with a final statement.
      </p>
      <p class="govuk-body">
        Required statement details that have not been verified are listed as launch blockers. They
        have not been guessed.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="app-section" aria-labelledby="scope-heading">
    <h2 class="govuk-heading-l" id="scope-heading">Scope and ownership</h2>
    <p class="govuk-body">
      This statement applies to <code>https://xgov-low-code.github.io/accessibility/</code>.
    </p>
    <p class="govuk-body">
      The accessibility statement and review process are owned by the Defra Power Platform Service
      Team and Defra Accessibility Team.
    </p>
    <p class="govuk-body">
      The statement must be reviewed before launch, after significant site changes, and at least
      every 12 months.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="app-section" aria-labelledby="current-evidence-heading">
    <h2 class="govuk-heading-l" id="current-evidence-heading">Current accessibility evidence</h2>
    <p class="govuk-body">
      The site is being checked against the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.2 AA
      standard.
    </p>
    <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
      <li>Automated axe checks cover the home page, catalogue and one generated detail page.</li>
      <li>Playwright smoke checks cover base-path routing, filters, detail pages and screenshot absence.</li>
      <li>The README includes manual keyboard, zoom, mobile, forced-colours and screen reader checks.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="govuk-body">
      A final compliance status has not yet been approved for publication.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="app-section" aria-labelledby="blockers-heading">
    <h2 class="govuk-heading-l" id="blockers-heading">Launch blockers for the final statement</h2>
    <div class="app-empty-state">
      <p class="govuk-body">
        The final accessibility statement must not be published until the statement owners have
        supplied or approved these details:
      </p>
      <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
        <li>compliance status against WCAG 2.2 AA</li>
        <li>known non-compliances, including WCAG references and fix plans, or confirmation that there are none</li>
        <li>any disproportionate burden or exempt content claims, or confirmation that there are none</li>
        <li>feedback and alternative-format contact details, including response expectations</li>
        <li>the relevant enforcement route for the publishing organisation</li>
        <li>final preparation date, review date and test date</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="app-section" aria-labelledby="feedback-heading">
    <h2 class="govuk-heading-l" id="feedback-heading">Feedback and contact information</h2>
    <p class="govuk-body">
      A public contact route for accessibility feedback and alternative-format requests has not yet
      been confirmed. This is a launch blocker for the final statement.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="app-section" aria-labelledby="enforcement-heading">
    <h2 class="govuk-heading-l" id="enforcement-heading">Enforcement route</h2>
    <p class="govuk-body">
      The final statement must include the relevant enforcement route required by public sector
      accessibility statement guidance. The route has not yet been confirmed for this site.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="app-section" aria-labelledby="guidance-heading">
    <h2 class="govuk-heading-l" id="guidance-heading">Guidance used</h2>
    <p class="govuk-body">
      This page was prepared using GOV.UK guidance on making websites accessible and publishing an
      accessibility statement, and the GOV.UK sample accessibility statement.
    </p>
    <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
      <li>
        <a
          class="govuk-link"
          href="https://www.gov.uk/guidance/make-your-website-or-app-accessible-and-publish-an-accessibility-statement"
        >
          Make your website or app accessible and publish an accessibility statement
        </a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          class="govuk-link"
          href="https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/sample-accessibility-statement"
        >
          Sample accessibility statement
        </a>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
